comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-04T21:32:43.246Z",codex-agent,"Both findings reproduced by inspection. The rejection handler previously called String(error), which throws for a null-prototype object before recording failure. It now wraps non-Error values using a constant diagnostic and preserves cause. runModelWorkerPool accepts an optional typed runner defaulting to the real worker; a barrier-controlled caller test asserts only the initial lanes start, active batches complete before rejection, and the original Error is retained. Real-process rejection and cleanup tests remain. Parent claim is retained; this child task owns only the review round."
  "2026-11-04T21:33:39.874Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in disposable source copies (reviewed files never mutated): restoring String(error) only in poolLanes fails the new unstringifiable-rejection test with TypeError: Cannot convert object to primitive value (0/1 pass). Replacing only the caller scheduling with eager Promise.all starts all 12 batches and fails the caller-stop assertion (0/1). Reverting only the caller runner invocation to runModelWorker fails the caller regression (0/1). Removing only poolLanes failure guard also fails the caller regression (0/1). Restored implementation passes both regressions (2/2), and the complete focused worker-budget suite passes 9/9. Typecheck and lint pass. Full PR self-review found no further instances of the coercion or caller-coverage defect classes in the changed code. dist is not tracked; full release builds regenerate it locally."
  "2026-11-04T21:34:59.772Z",codex-agent,"Initial npm release attempt correctly rejected duplicated promise-barrier setup at the unchanged zero-duplication threshold. Replaced that setup with Promise.withResolvers; duplication now 0% (0 clone pairs, 144 sources). Both new regressions pass again. Strict pm health passes with isolated HOME/Git config; the ordinary host check reported only a global pm-github host-version skew, so no dependency pin or telemetry setting was changed. Running complete npm and Bun release gates serially with PM_MEMORY_WORKER_POOL=2 and isolated HOME/Git config."
  "2026-11-04T21:39:33.663Z",codex-agent,"Final focused runtime checks: PM_MEMORY_WORKER_POOL=2 node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/worker-budget.test.ts passed 9/9 through the linked-test runner; PM_MEMORY_WORKER_POOL=2 bun test --max-concurrency=2 test/worker-budget.test.ts passed 9/9. npm release:check has passed identity, typecheck, lint, duplication (0%), build and docstring (44 files, 168 declarations); full coverage is running without failures so far. Full npm/Bun release gates remain pending, not passed. Pushing the reviewed fixes now starts the CI release matrix; observe the queue rule 30-minute CI waiting limit. No extra findings, thread replies, resolutions, merges or releases."
  "2026-11-04T21:40:31.518Z",codex-agent,"Implementation pushed as 206b056b1b9c236cc4a57f858c36202f2c97714c. CI run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions/runs/41918170950 . Release matrix legs (22 npm, 26 npm, 26 Bun) are queued; 0/3 complete gates confirmed on that head. Current branch checks: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/48/checks . Focused checks are 9/9 Node and 9/9 Bun; all four mutation checks fail as expected and restored regressions pass 2/2. No local full-suite failure has occurred since fixing the initial duplication finding. Local complete npm coverage and subsequent Bun gate are not yet complete. The previous CI required about four hours; if full gates remain pending at the queue rule 30-minute observation cutoff, report them as pending and stop local test descendants before finishing. This final evidence-only tracker commit will start fresh exact-head CI; do not count prior-head successful runs as final-head verification."
  "2026-11-04T22:00:36.432Z",codex-agent,"Final local results: linked Node worker-budget rerun passed 9/9 on the final source; native Bun worker-budget passed 9/9; npm run test:install passed 2/2 real packed consumers (npm and Bun) with isolated HOME/Git configuration. Production audit found 0 vulnerabilities; pack dry-run included 118 allowed files; publish attestation, changelog, static gates and isolated strict pm health pass. The duplicate local full npm gate was deliberately interrupted: 144 passed, 0 failed, 55 cancelled; it is incomplete, not a passed gate or a host-load timeout. All 13 release-gate child processes were stopped and verified inactive before separate packed acceptance ran. Bun full release did not start locally after that interruption. Full release verification remains pending in CI: 0/3 legs complete, current observed run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions/runs/41918358959 . Superseded implementation-only run 41918170950 was cancelled; neither that run nor old successful heads is counted as final-head evidence. Latest final-head checks will remain at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/48/checks after this evidence-only commit. Both review threads were fetched again with every comment; still only the same two unresolved findings, no outside-diff section, and no thread replies or resolutions. No pm CLI defect was encountered; ordinary host health version skew disappears with isolated HOME, without pin or telemetry changes."
